# GitHub API Commit Pattern — PlasticOS

This repo lives inside Dropbox. Local `git checkout`, `git mktree`, and pack-file operations frequently fail with `mmap failed: Operation timed out` or SIGBUS (signal 10). When this happens, use the GitHub API directly.

## Get the Token First

```bash
GH_TOKEN=$(echo "url=https://github.com" | git credential fill | grep password | cut -d= -f2)
```

## Commit a File Change via API

```bash
# 1. Get current file SHA on the target branch
FILE_SHA=$(curl -s "https://api.github.com/repos/cryptoxdog/IB-Odoo_19/contents/PATH/TO/FILE?ref=BRANCH" \
  | python3 -c "import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['sha'])")

# 2. Prepare base64-encoded new content
NEW_CONTENT=$(python3 -c "
import base64
content = open('PATH/TO/FILE').read()
print(base64.b64encode(content.encode()).decode())
")

# 3. Commit via API
curl -s -X PUT "https://api.github.com/repos/cryptoxdog/IB-Odoo_19/contents/PATH/TO/FILE" \
  -H "Authorization: token $GH_TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d "{\"message\":\"fix: description\",\"content\":\"$NEW_CONTENT\",\"sha\":\"$FILE_SHA\",\"branch\":\"BRANCH\"}" \
  | python3 -c "import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print('OK:', d.get('commit',{}).get('sha','ERROR'), d.get('message',''))"
```

## When to Use This

- `git checkout <branch>` fails with mmap/SIGBUS
- `git mktree` or `git commit-tree` times out
- `index.lock` keeps reappearing (Dropbox interference)
- Branching to a remote branch without local checkout

## Permanent Fix (do when convenient)

Move repo out of Dropbox — the git object store should never be inside Dropbox:
```bash
mv "/Users/macm2/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/Repo_Dropbox_IB/IB-Odoo_19" ~/dev/IB-Odoo_19
```
GitHub is already the source of truth. Dropbox sync of `.git/` is redundant and harmful.

## Branch Model

- **`Staging`** = dev branch (all PRs target this)
- **`Production`** = prod/main (promote from Staging when CI is green)
- Never merge feature branches directly to `Production`
